\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 \ul \ulc0 ISSUE 1: Handling for Empty or Whitespace-Only Input\

\f1\b0 \ulnone \

\f0\b Problem: 
\f1\b0 If a user runs the tool without providing any input (e.g., meeting notes), whether via a file or directly in the terminal, the script will pass an empty string to the Claude API, which wastes API credits and returns a blank, useless report. There aren\'92t sufficient guards to prevent pass-through of empty or whitespace-only strings.\
\

\f0\b Fix:
\f1\b0  We\'92ll need to make three code changes throughout the script to accommodate this validation - the first for a totally blank file or input in the initial read of the file, the second and third changes for handling blank team sections in multi-team parsing of the file (mid-script).
\f0\b  
\f1\b0 \
\

