\f0\b Takeaway: 
\f1\b0 The tool\'92s current design has high preference for markdown (.md) files, which are typically used by more technically-oriented users. To accommodate the less technically-inclined, we built a template for those users so they can still make use of the tool - avoiding far more complex code changes for these early iterations of the tool (additional file types and formats are on the roadmap for later). We also eliminated a future issue by making the parsing of markdown format more resilient to user input in case an additional H2 line (\'93## \'93) is entered elsewhere in the file. \
